We were walking down the sidewalk in Tempe, AZ, at
the usual speed of elders.

We were overtaken by a nicely dressed young man.

Over his shoulder, hanging from a single strap, he
wore a fairly big gray leather tote, with a flap
closure over the top.

Upon that flap appeared the sewn label, white on
black:

                    Bag of Holding

That cracked me right up, and then of course I had
to explain the joke to my D&D-naive spouse-alike.

I hope someone here knows where such a tote can be
purchased.

What a nice tribal totem object it is.

